    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35580" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per-stŭdĭōsus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>very desirous</i>, <i>very
				fond</i> of any thing: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">musicorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Tusc. 5, 22, 63</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">litterarum Graecarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Sen. 1</span></i>
			
			<i>fin.—Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perstŭdĭōsē</span></b> , <i>very eagerly</i>, <i>very fondly</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">audire aliquem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Brut. 56, 207</span></i>
			.</div>
